FFmpeg: never pick Amlogic FBC (AM21C/AM21B) capture formats

The meson-amvdec driver offers compressed AM21C as its only 10-bit
capture format. Only the meson VPU overlay can display it; the player
renders through the GPU (mpv's EGL dmabuf interop), which shows a blue
picture, and copying back to memory fails. Skipping it makes FFmpeg fall
back to NV12M, which the decoder writes with Main 10 downsampled to 8 bits.

--- a/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
+++ b/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
@@ -393,6 +393,17 @@
 
     // Next try to use the first known format with matching bit depth
     while (ioctl(fctxi->video_fd, VIDIOC_ENUM_FMT, &fmtdesc) >= 0) {
+        /*
+         * Amlogic FBC can only be shown by the meson VPU video overlay, not
+         * by a GPU: take the linear NV12M the decoder also writes (Main 10
+         * downsampled to 8 bits) instead.
+         */
+        if (fmtdesc.pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_MESON_AM21C ||
+            fmtdesc.pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_MESON_AM21B) {
+            fmtdesc.index++;
+            continue;
+        }
+
         for (int i = 0; i < FF_ARRAY_ELEMS(v4l2request_capture_pixelformats); i++) {
             if (fmtdesc.pixelformat == v4l2request_capture_pixelformats[i].pixelformat) {
                 if (fctx->bit_depth == v4l2request_capture_pixelformats[i].bit_depth ||
